**Electricity Ray (Su):** An arrowhawk can fire this ray once per round, with a range of 50 feet.','{"full_attack":"Electricity ray +19 ranged touch (2d8) or bite +20 melee (2d6+9)","environment":"Elemental Plane of Air","organization":"Solitary or clutch (2–4)","treasure":"None","advancement":"16–24 HD (Large); 25–32 HD (Gargantuan)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"15d8+45 (112 hp)","hit_points":112,"base_attack_grapple":"+15/+25","attack":"Electricity ray +19 ranged touch (2d8) or bite +21 melee (2d6+9)","full_attack":"Electricity ray +19 ranged touch (2d8) or bite +20 melee (2d6+9)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +12, Ref +14, Will +10","abilities":{"str":"22","dex":"21","con":"16","int":"10","wis":"13","cha":"13"},"skills":"Diplomacy +3, Escape Artist +23, Knowledge (the planes) +18, Listen +21, Move Silently +23, Search +18, Sense Motive +19, Spot +21, Survival +19 (+21 following tracks, +21 Plane of Air), Use Rope +5 (+7 involving bindings)","feats":"Alertness, Blind-Fight, Combat Reflexes, Dodge, Flyby Attack, Weapon Finesse, Weapon Focus (bite)B","special_attacks":"Electricity ray","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., immunity to acid, electricity, and poison, resistance to cold 10 and fire 10"},"source_file":"monsters-intro-a.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-intro-a.html',true),
('assassin_vine','Assassin Vine','Assassin Vine','3','Large','Plant','Always neutral','4d8+12 (30 hp)',30,'+0','5 ft. (1 square)','15 (–1 size, +6 natural), touch 9, flat-footed 15','+3/+12','Slam +7 melee (1d6+7)','10 ft./10 ft. (20 ft. with vine)','+7','+1','+2',20,10,16,null,13,9,'','','{"special_attacks":"Constrict 1d6+7, entangle, improved grab","special_qualities":"Blindsight 30 ft., camouflage, immunity to electricity, low-light vision, plant traits, resistance to cold 10 and fire 10"}'::jsonb,'The assassin vine is a semi-mobile plant that collects its own grisly fertilizer by grabbing and crushing animals and depositing the carcasses near its roots.

A mature plant consists of a main vine, about 20 feet long. Smaller vines up to 5 feet long branch off from the main vine about every 6 inches. These small vines bear clusters of leaves, and in late summer they produce bunches of small fruits that resemble wild grapes. The fruit is tough and has a hearty but bitter flavor. Assassin vine berries make a heady wine.

An assassin vine can move about, albeit very slowly, but usually stays put unless it needs to seek prey in a new vicinity.

A subterranean version of the assassin vine grows near hot springs, volcanic vents, and other sources of thermal energy. These plants have thin, wiry stems and gray leaves shot through with silver, brown, and white veins so that they resemble mineral deposits. An assassin vine growing underground usually generates enough offal to support a thriving colony of mushrooms and other fungi, which spring up around the plant and help conceal it.

### Combat

An assassin vine uses simple tactics:

It lies still until prey comes within reach, then attacks. It uses its entangle ability both to catch prey and to deter counterattacks.

**Constrict (Ex):** An assassin vine deals 1d6+7 points of damage with a successful grapple check.

**Entangle (Su):** An assassin vine can animate plants within 30 feet of itself as a free action (Ref DC 13 partial).

The effect lasts until the vine dies or decides to end it (also a free action). The save DC is Wisdom-based. The ability is otherwise similar to _entangle_ (caster level 4th).

**Improved Grab (Ex):** To use this ability, an assassin vine must hit with its slam attack.

It can then attempt to start a grapple as a free action without provoking an attack of opportunity.

If it wins the grapple check, it establishes a hold and can constrict.

**Blindsight (Ex):** Assassin vines have no visual organs but can ascertain all foes within 30 feet using sound, scent, and vibration.

**Camouflage (Ex):** Since an assassin vine looks like a normal plant when at rest, it takes a DC 20 Spot check to notice it before it attacks.

Anyone with ranks in Survival or Knowledge (nature) can use one of those skills instead of Spot to notice the plant. Dwarves can use stonecunning to notice the subterranean version.','{"full_attack":"Slam +7 melee (1d6+7)","environment":"Temperate forests","organization":"Solitary or patch (2–4)","treasure":"1/10th coins; 50% goods; 50% items","advancement":"5–16 HD (Huge); 17–32 HD (Gargantuan); 33+ HD (Colossal)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"4d8+12 (30 hp)","hit_points":30,"base_attack_grapple":"+3/+12","attack":"Slam +7 melee (1d6+7)","full_attack":"Slam +7 melee (1d6+7)","space_reach":"10 ft./10 ft. (20 ft. with vine)","saves":"Fort +7, Ref +1, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"20","dex":"10","con":"16","int":null,"wis":"13","cha":"9"},"skills":"","feats":"","special_attacks":"Constrict 1d6+7, entangle, improved grab","special_qualities":"Blindsight 30 ft., camouflage, immunity to electricity, low-light vision, plant traits, resistance to cold 10 and fire 10"},"source_file":"monsters-intro-a.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-intro-a.html',true),
('athach','Athach','Athach','8','Huge','Aberration','Often chaotic evil','14d8+70 (133 hp)',133,'+1','35 ft. in hide armor (7 squares); base speed 50 ft.','20 (–2 size, +1 Dex, +3 hide armor, +8 natural), touch 9, flat-footed 19','+10/+26 Attack:Morningstar +16 melee (3d6+8) or rock +9 ranged (2d6+8)','','15 ft./15 ft.','+9','+5','+10',26,13,21,7,12,6,'Climb +9, Jump +18, Listen +7, Spot +7','Alertness, Cleave, Multiweapon Fighting, Power Attack, Weapon Focus (bite)','{"special_attacks":"Poison","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft."}'::jsonb,'The athach is a hulking, misshapen biped. An adult stands some 18 feet tall and weighs about 4,500 pounds. Athachs speak a crude dialect of Giant.

### Combat

Athachs charge into melee combat unless their opponents are out of reach, in which case they throw rocks. They sometimes try to overrun armored opponents to reach unarmored opponents in back ranks. With its first few melee attacks, an athach tends to flail about indiscriminately. After a few rounds, it concentrates on foes that have been hitting it most often and uses its bite on whoever has dealt it the most damage.

**Poison (Ex):** Injury, Fortitude DC 22, initial damage 1d6 Str, secondary damage 2d6 Str. The save DC is Constitution-based.','{"full_attack":"Morningstar +12/+7 melee (3d6+8), and 2 morningstars +12 melee (3d6+4), and bite +12 melee (2d8+4 plus poison); or rock +5 ranged (2d6+8), and 2 rocks +5 ranged (2d6+4)","environment":"Temperate hills","organization":"Solitary, gang (2–4), or tribe (7–12)","treasure":"1/2 coins; double goods; standard items","advancement":"15–28 HD (Huge)","level_adjustment":"+5","statblock":{"hit_dice":"14d8+70 (133 hp)","hit_points":133,"base_attack_grapple":"+10/+26 Attack:Morningstar +16 melee (3d6+8) or rock +9 ranged (2d6+8)","attack":"","full_attack":"Morningstar +12/+7 melee (3d6+8), and 2 morningstars +12 melee (3d6+4), and bite +12 melee (2d8+4 plus poison); or rock +5 ranged (2d6+8), and 2 rocks +5 ranged (2d6+4)","space_reach":"15 ft./15 ft.","saves":"Fort +9, Ref +5, Will +10","abilities":{"str":"26","dex":"13","con":"21","int":"7","wis":"12","cha":"6"},"skills":"Climb +9, Jump +18, Listen +7, Spot +7","feats":"Alertness, Cleave, Multiweapon Fighting, Power Attack, Weapon Focus (bite)","special_attacks":"Poison","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft."},"source_file":"monsters-intro-a.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-intro-a.html',true),
('avoral','Avoral','Avoral','9','Medium','Outsider (Extraplanar, Good)','Always neutral good','7d8+35 (66 hp)',66,'+6','40 ft. (8 squares), fly 90 ft. (good)','24 (+6 Dex, +8 natural), touch 16, flat-footed 18','+7/+9','Claw +13 melee (2d6+2) or wing +13 melee (2d8+2)','5 ft./5 ft.','+10','+11','+8',15,23,20,15,16,16,'Bluff +13, Concentration +15, Diplomacy +7, Disguise +3 (+5 acting), Handle Animal +13, Hide +16, Intimidate +5, Knowledge (any one) +12, Listen +13, Move Silently +16, Ride +8, Sense Motive +13, Spellcraft +12, Spot +21','Empower Spell-Like Ability (magic missile), Flyby Attack, Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"Spell-like abilities, fear aura","special_qualities":"Damage reduction 10/evil or silver, darkvision 60 ft., immunity to electricity and petrification, lay on hands, low-light vision, resistance to cold 10 and sonic 10, speak with animals, spell resistance 25, true seeing"}'::jsonb,'An avoral’s bones are strong but hollow, so even the largest specimens weigh no more than 120 pounds. An avoral is about 7 feet tall. Each of an avoral’s wings has a small hand at the midpoint. When the wings are folded, these appendages are about where human hands would be and can do nearly anything hands can do.

An avoral’s visual acuity is virtually unmatched: It can see detail on objects up to 10 miles away and is said to be able to discern the color of a creature’s eyes at 200 paces.

Avorals speak Celestial, Infernal, and Draconic, but can speak with almost any creature, thanks to their _tongues_ ability.

### Combat

On the ground, an avoral can lash out with its wings to deliver punishing blows. However, it prefers to meet its foes in the air, where it can employ its talons and make full use of its aerial speed and agility. It can’t make wing attacks while flying, however.

An avoral’s natural weapons, as well as any weapons it wields, are treated as good-aligned for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.

**Spell-Like Abilities:** At will—_aid, blur_ (self only), _command_ (DC 14), _detect magic, dimension door, dispel magic, gust of wind_ (DC 15), _hold person_ (DC 16), _light, magic circle against evil_ (self only), _magic missile, see invisibility;_ 3/day—_lightning bolt_ (DC 16). Caster level 8th. The save DCs are Charisma-based.

**Fear Aura (Su):** Once per day an avoral can create an aura of fear in a 20-foot radius. It is otherwise identical with _fear_ from an 8th-level caster (save DC 17). The save DC is Charisma-based.

**Lay on Hands (Su):** As the paladin class feature, except that each day, an avoral can heal an amount of damage equal to its full normal hit points.

**Speak with Animals (Su):** This ability works like _speak with animals_ (caster level 8th) but is a free action and does not require sound.

**True Seeing (Su):** This ability is identical with _true seeing_ (caster level 14th), except that it has personal range and the avoral must concentrate for 1 full round before it takes effect. Thereafter the ability remains in effect as long as the avoral concentrates on it.

**Skills:** An avoral’s sharp eyes give it a +8 racial bonus on Spot checks.','{"full_attack":"2 claws +13 melee (2d6+2) or 2 wings +13 melee (2d8+2)","environment":"A good-aligned plane.","organization":"Solitary, pair, or squad (3–5)","treasure":"No coins; double goods; standard items","advancement":"8–14 HD (Medium); 15–21 HD (Large)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"7d8+35 (66 hp)","hit_points":66,"base_attack_grapple":"+7/+9","attack":"Claw +13 melee (2d6+2) or wing +13 melee (2d8+2)","full_attack":"2 claws +13 melee (2d6+2) or 2 wings +13 melee (2d8+2)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +10 (+14 against poison), Ref +11, Will +8","abilities":{"str":"15","dex":"23","con":"20","int":"15","wis":"16","cha":"16"},"skills":"Bluff +13, Concentration +15, Diplomacy +7, Disguise +3 (+5 acting), Handle Animal +13, Hide +16, Intimidate +5, Knowledge (any one) +12, Listen +13, Move Silently +16, Ride +8, Sense Motive +13, Spellcraft +12, Spot +21","feats":"Empower Spell-Like Ability (magic missile), Flyby Attack, Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"Spell-like abilities, fear aura","special_qualities":"Damage reduction 10/evil or silver, darkvision 60 ft., immunity to electricity and petrification, lay on hands, low-light vision, resistance to cold 10 and sonic 10, speak with animals, spell resistance 25, true seeing"},"source_file":"monsters-intro-a.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-intro-a.html',true),
('azer','Azer','Azer','2','Medium','Outsider (Extraplanar, Fire)','Always lawful neutral','2d8+2 (11 hp)',11,'+1','20 ft. in scale mail (4 squares); base speed 30 ft.','23 (+1 Dex, +6 natural, +4 scale mail, +2 heavy','+2/+3','Warhammer +3 melee (1d8+1/x3 plus 1 fire) or shortspear +3 ranged (1d6+1 plus 1 fire)','5 ft./5 ft.','+4','+4','+4',13,13,13,12,12,9,'Appraise +6, Climb +0, Craft (any two) +6, Hide +0, Jump –6, Listen +6, Search +6, Spot +6','Power Attack','{"special_attacks":"Heat","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., immunity to fire, spell resistance 13, vulnerability to cold"}'::jsonb,'Azers are dwarflike beings native to the Elemental Plane of Fire. They wear kilts of brass, bronze, or copper, and speak Ignan and Common.

### Combat

Azers use broad-headed spears or well-crafted hammers in combat. When unarmed, they attempt to grapple foes.

Although unfriendly and taciturn, azers rarely provoke a fight except to relieve a foe of gems, which they love. If threatened, they fight to the death, but they see the value of taking prisoners themselves.

**Heat (Ex):** An azer’s body is intensely hot, so its unarmed attacks deal extra fire damage. Its metallic weapons also conduct this heat.

### Azers as Characters

Azer characters possess the following racial traits.

— +2 Strength, +2 Dexterity, +2 Constitution, +2 Intelligence, +2 Wisdom, –2 Charisma.

—Medium size.

—An azer’s base land speed is 30 feet.

—Darkvision: Azers can see in the dark up to 60 feet.

—Racial Hit Dice: An azer begins with two levels of outsider, which provide 2d8 Hit Dice, a base attack bonus of +2, and base saving throw bonuses of Fort +3, Ref +3, and Will +3.

—Racial Skills: An azer’s outsider levels give it skill points equal to 5 x (8 + Int modifier). Its class skills are Appraise, Climb, Craft, Hide, Jump, Listen, Search, and Spot.

—Racial Feats: An azer’s outsider levels give it one feat.

— +6 natural armor bonus.

—Special Attacks (see above): Heat.

—Special Qualities (see above): Immunity to fire, spell resistance equal to 13 + class levels, vulnerability to cold.

—Automatic Languages: Common, Ignan. Bonus Languages: Abyssal, Aquan, Auran, Celestial, Infernal, Terran.

—Favored Class: Fighter.

—Level adjustment +4.','{"full_attack":"Warhammer +3 melee (1d8+1/x3 plus 1 fire) or shortspear +3 ranged (1d6+1 plus 1 fire)","environment":"Elemental Plane of Fire","organization":"Solitary, pair, team (3–4), squad (11–20 plus 2 3rd-level sergeants and 1 leader of 3rd–6th level), or clan (30–100 plus 50% noncombatants plus 1 3rd-level sergeant per 20 adults, 5 5th-level lieutenants, and 3 7th-level captains)","treasure":"Standard coins; double goods (nonflammables only); standard items (nonflammables only)","advancement":"By character class","level_adjustment":"+4","statblock":{"hit_dice":"2d8+2 (11 hp)","hit_points":11,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+3","attack":"Warhammer +3 melee (1d8+1/x3 plus 1 fire) or shortspear +3 ranged (1d6+1 plus 1 fire)","full_attack":"Warhammer +3 melee (1d8+1/x3 plus 1 fire) or shortspear +3 ranged (1d6+1 plus 1 fire)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +4, Ref +4, Will +4","abilities":{"str":"13","dex":"13","con":"13","int":"12","wis":"12","cha":"9"},"skills":"Appraise +6, Climb +0, Craft (any two) +6, Hide +0, Jump –6, Listen +6, Search +6, Spot +6","feats":"Power Attack","special_attacks":"Heat","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., immunity to fire, spell resistance 13, vulnerability to cold"},"source_file":"monsters-intro-a.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-intro-a.html',true),
('ape','Ape','Ape','2','Large','Animal','','4d8+11 (29 hp)',29,'+2','30 ft. (6 squares), climb 30 ft.','14 (–1 size, +2 Dex, +3 natural), touch 11, flat-footed 12','+3/+12','Claws +7 melee (1d6+5)','10 ft./10 ft.','+6','+6','+2',21,15,14,2,12,7,'Climb +14, Listen +6, Spot +6','Alertness, Toughness','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'These powerful omnivores resemble gorillas but are far more aggressive; they kill and eat anything they can catch. An adult male ape is 5-1/2 to 6 feet tall and weighs 300 to 400 pounds.

### Combat

**Skills:** Apes have a +8 racial bonus on Climb checks and can always choose to take 10 on Climb checks, even if rushed or threatened.','{"full_attack":"2 claws +7 melee (1d6+5) and bite +2 melee (1d6+2)","environment":"Warm forests","organization":"Solitary, pair, or company (3–5)","treasure":"","advancement":"5–8 HD (Large)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"4d8+11 (29 hp)","hit_points":29,"base_attack_grapple":"+3/+12","attack":"Claws +7 melee (1d6+5)","full_attack":"2 claws +7 melee (1d6+5) and bite +2 melee (1d6+2)","space_reach":"10 ft./10 ft.","saves":"Fort +6, Ref +6, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"21","dex":"15","con":"14","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"7"},"skills":"Climb +14, Listen +6, Spot +6","feats":"Alertness, Toughness","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('baboon','Baboon','Baboon','1/2','Medium','Animal','','1d8+1 (5 hp)',5,'+2','40 ft. (8 squares), climb 30 ft.','13 (+2 Dex, +1 natural), touch 12, flat-footed 11','+0/+2','Bite +2 melee (1d6+3)','5 ft./5 ft.','+3','+4','+1',15,14,12,2,12,4,'Climb +10, Listen +5, Spot +5','Alertness','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'Baboons are powerful and aggressive primates adapted to life on the ground. They prefer open spaces but climb trees to find safe places to rest overnight. A typical baboon is the size of a big dog.

Males can be 2 to 4 feet long and weigh as much as 90 pounds.

### Combat

Baboons usually attack in groups.

**Skills:** Baboons have a +8 racial bonus on Climb checks and can always choose to take 10 on Climb checks, even if rushed or threatened.','{"full_attack":"Bite +2 melee (1d6+3)","environment":"Warm plains","organization":"Solitary or troop (10–40)","treasure":"","advancement":"2–3 HD (Medium)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1d8+1 (5 hp)","hit_points":5,"base_attack_grapple":"+0/+2","attack":"Bite +2 melee (1d6+3)","full_attack":"Bite +2 melee (1d6+3)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +3, Ref +4, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"15","dex":"14","con":"12","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"4"},"skills":"Climb +10, Listen +5, Spot +5","feats":"Alertness","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('badger','Badger','Badger','1/2','Small','Animal','','1d8+2 (6 hp)',6,'+3','30 ft. (6 squares), burrow 10 ft.','15 (+1 size, +3 Dex, +1 natural), touch 14, flat-footed 12','+0/–5','Claw +4 melee (1d2–1)','5 ft./5 ft.','+4','+5','+1',8,17,15,2,12,6,'Escape Artist +7, Listen +3, Spot +3','TrackB, Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"Rage","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'The badger is a furry animal with a squat, powerful body. Its strong forelimbs are armed with long claws for digging. An adult badger is 2 to 3 feet long and weighs 25 to 35 pounds.

### Combat

Badgers attack with their sharp claws and teeth.

**Rage (Ex):** A badger that takes damage in combat flies into a berserk rage on its next turn, clawing and biting madly until either it or its opponent is dead. It gains +4 to Strength, +4 to Constitution, and –2 to Armor Class. The creature cannot end its rage voluntarily.

**Skills:** A badger has a +4 racial bonus on Escape Artist checks.','{"full_attack":"2 claws +4 melee (1d2–1) and bite –1 melee (1d3–1)","environment":"Temperate forests","organization":"Solitary, pair, or cete (3–5)","treasure":"","advancement":"2 HD (Small)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1d8+2 (6 hp)","hit_points":6,"base_attack_grapple":"+0/–5","attack":"Claw +4 melee (1d2–1)","full_attack":"2 claws +4 melee (1d2–1) and bite –1 melee (1d3–1)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +4, Ref +5, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"8","dex":"17","con":"15","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"6"},"skills":"Escape Artist +7, Listen +3, Spot +3","feats":"TrackB, Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"Rage","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('bat','Morcego','Bat','1/10','Diminutive','Animal','','1/4 d8 (1 hp)',1,'+2','5 ft (1 square), fly 40 ft. (good)','16 (+4 size, +2 Dex), touch 16, flat-footed 14','+0/–17','—','1 ft./0 ft.','+2','+4','+2',1,15,10,2,14,4,'Hide +14, Listen +8*, Move Silently +6, Spot +8*','Alertness','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Blindsense 20 ft., low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'Bats are nocturnal flying mammals. The statistics presented here describe small, insectivorous bats.

### Combat

Blindsense (Ex): A bat notices and locates creatures within 20 feet. Opponents still have 100% concealment against a creature with blindsense.

Skills: \*A bat has a +4 racial bonus on Spot and Listen checks. These bonuses are lost if its blindsense is negated.','{"full_attack":"—","environment":"Temperate deserts","organization":"Colony (10–40) or crowd (10–50)","treasure":"","advancement":"—","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1/4 d8 (1 hp)","hit_points":1,"base_attack_grapple":"+0/–17","attack":"—","full_attack":"—","space_reach":"1 ft./0 ft.","saves":"Fort +2, Ref +4, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"1","dex":"15","con":"10","int":"2","wis":"14","cha":"4"},"skills":"Hide +14, Listen +8*, Move Silently +6, Spot +8*","feats":"Alertness","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Blindsense 20 ft., low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('bear_black','Bear, Black','Bear, Black','2','Medium','Animal','','3d8+6 (19 hp)',19,'+1','40 ft. (8 squares)','13 (+1 Dex, +2 natural), touch 11, flat-footed 12','+2/+6','Claw +6 melee (1d4+4)','5 ft./5 ft.','+5','+4','+2',19,13,15,2,12,6,'Climb +4, Listen +4, Spot +4, Swim +8','Endurance, Run','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'The black bear is a forest-dwelling omnivore that usually is not dangerous unless an interloper threatens its cubs or food supply.

Black bears can be pure black, blond, or cinnamon in color and are rarely more than 5 feet long.

### Combat

Black bears rip prey with their claws and teeth.

**Skills:** A black bear has a +4 racial bonus on Swim checks.','{"full_attack":"2 claws +6 melee (1d4+4) and bite +1 melee (1d6+2)","environment":"Temperate forests","organization":"Solitary or pair","treasure":"","advancement":"4–5 HD (Medium)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"3d8+6 (19 hp)","hit_points":19,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+6","attack":"Claw +6 melee (1d4+4)","full_attack":"2 claws +6 melee (1d4+4) and bite +1 melee (1d6+2)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +5, Ref +4, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"19","dex":"13","con":"15","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"6"},"skills":"Climb +4, Listen +4, Spot +4, Swim +8","feats":"Endurance, Run","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('bear_brown','Bear, Brown','Bear, Brown','4','Large','Animal','','6d8+24 (51 hp)',51,'+1','40 ft. (8 squares)','15 (–1 size, +1 Dex, +5 natural), touch 10, flat-footed 14','+4/+16','Claw +11 melee (1d8+8)','10 ft./5 ft.','+9','+6','+3',27,13,19,2,12,6,'Listen +4, Spot +7, Swim +12','Endurance, Run, Track','{"special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'These massive carnivores weigh more than 1,800 pounds and stand nearly 9 feet tall when they rear up on their hind legs. They are bad-tempered and territorial. The brown bear’s statistics can be used for almost any big bear, including the grizzly.

### Combat

A brown bear attacks mainly by tearing at opponents with its claws.

**Improved Grab (Ex):** To use this ability, a brown bear must hit with a claw attack. It can then attempt to start a grapple as a free action without provoking an attack of opportunity.

**Skills:** A brown bear has a +4 racial bonus on Swim checks.','{"full_attack":"2 claws +11 melee (1d8+8) and bite +6 melee (2d6+4)","environment":"Cold forests","organization":"Solitary or pair","treasure":"","advancement":"7–10 HD (Large)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"6d8+24 (51 hp)","hit_points":51,"base_attack_grapple":"+4/+16","attack":"Claw +11 melee (1d8+8)","full_attack":"2 claws +11 melee (1d8+8) and bite +6 melee (2d6+4)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +9, Ref +6, Will +3","abilities":{"str":"27","dex":"13","con":"19","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"6"},"skills":"Listen +4, Spot +7, Swim +12","feats":"Endurance, Run, Track","special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('bear_polar','Bear, Polar','Bear, Polar','4','Large','Animal','','8d8+32 (68 hp)',68,'+1','40 ft. (8 squares), swim 30 ft.','15 (–1 size, +1 Dex, +5 natural), touch 10, flat-footed 14','+6/+18','Claw +13 (1d8+8)','10 ft./5 ft.','+10','+7','+3',27,13,19,2,12,6,'Hide –2*, Listen +5, Spot +7, Swim +16','Endurance, Run, Track','{"special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'These long, lean carnivores are slightly taller than brown bears.

### Combat

Polar bears fight just as brown bears do.

**Improved Grab (Ex):** To use this ability, a polar bear must hit with a claw attack. It can then attempt to start a grapple as a free action without provoking an attack of opportunity.

**Skills:** A polar bear has a +8 racial bonus on any Swim check to perform some special action or avoid a hazard. It can always choose to take 10 on a Swim check, even if distracted or endangered. It can use the run action while swimming, provided it swims in a straight line. \*A polar bear’s white coat bestows a +12 racial bonus on Hide checks in snowy areas.','{"full_attack":"2 claws +13 melee (1d8+8) and bite +8 melee (2d6+4)","environment":"Cold plains","organization":"Solitary or pair","treasure":"","advancement":"9–12 HD (Large)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"8d8+32 (68 hp)","hit_points":68,"base_attack_grapple":"+6/+18","attack":"Claw +13 (1d8+8)","full_attack":"2 claws +13 melee (1d8+8) and bite +8 melee (2d6+4)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +10, Ref +7, Will +3","abilities":{"str":"27","dex":"13","con":"19","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"6"},"skills":"Hide –2*, Listen +5, Spot +7, Swim +16","feats":"Endurance, Run, Track","special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('bison','Bison','Bison','2','Large','Animal','','5d8+15 (37 hp)',37,'+0','40 ft. (8 squares)','13 (–1 size, +4 natural), touch 9, flat-footed 13','+3/+13','Gore +8 melee (1d8+9)','10 ft./5 ft.','+7','+4','+1',22,10,16,2,11,4,'Listen +7, Spot +5','Alertness, Endurance','{"special_attacks":"Stampede","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'These herd animals can be aggressive when protecting young and during the mating season, but they generally prefer flight to fighting. A bison stands more than 6 feet tall at the shoulder and is 9 to 12 feet long. It weigh 1,800 to 2,400 pounds. The bison’s statistics can be used for almost any large herd animal.

### Combat

**Stampede (Ex):** A frightened herd of bison flees as a group in a random direction (but always away from the perceived source of danger). They literally run over anything of Large size or smaller that gets in their way, dealing 1d12 points of damage for each five bison in the herd (Reflex DC 18 half ). The save DC is Strength-based.','{"full_attack":"Gore +8 melee (1d8+9)","environment":"Temperate plains","organization":"Solitary or herd (6–30)","treasure":"","advancement":"6–7 HD (Large)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"5d8+15 (37 hp)","hit_points":37,"base_attack_grapple":"+3/+13","attack":"Gore +8 melee (1d8+9)","full_attack":"Gore +8 melee (1d8+9)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +7, Ref +4, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"22","dex":"10","con":"16","int":"2","wis":"11","cha":"4"},"skills":"Listen +7, Spot +5","feats":"Alertness, Endurance","special_attacks":"Stampede","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('boar','Boar','Boar','2','Medium','Animal','','3d8+12 (25 hp)',25,'+0','40 ft. (8 squares)','16 (+6 natural), touch 10, flat-footed 16','+2/+4','Gore +4 melee (1d8+3)','5 ft./5 ft.','+6','+3','+2',15,10,17,2,13,4,'Listen +7, Spot +5','Alertness, Toughness','{"special_attacks":"Ferocity","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'Though not carnivores, these wild swine are bad-tempered and usually charge anyone who disturbs them. A boar is covered in coarse, grayish-black fur. Adult males are about 4 feet long and 3 feet high at the shoulder.

### Combat

**Ferocity (Ex):** A boar is such a tenacious combatant that it continues to fight without penalty even while disabled or dying.','{"full_attack":"Gore +4 melee (1d8+3)","environment":"Temperate forests","organization":"Solitary or herd (5–8)","treasure":"","advancement":"4–5 HD (Medium)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"3d8+12 (25 hp)","hit_points":25,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+4","attack":"Gore +4 melee (1d8+3)","full_attack":"Gore +4 melee (1d8+3)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +6, Ref +3, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"15","dex":"10","con":"17","int":"2","wis":"13","cha":"4"},"skills":"Listen +7, Spot +5","feats":"Alertness, Toughness","special_attacks":"Ferocity","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('camel','Camel','Camel','1','Large','Animal','','3d8+6 (19 hp)',19,'+3','50 ft. (10 squares)','13 (–1 size, +3 Dex, +1 natural) touch 12, flat-footed 10','+2/+10','Bite +0 melee (1d4+2*)','10 ft./5 ft.','+5','+6','+1',18,16,14,2,11,4,'Listen +5, Spot +5','Alertness, Endurance','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'Camels are known for their ability to travel long distances without food or water.

The statistics presented here are for the dromedary, or one-humped camel, which thrives in warm deserts. A dromedary stands about 7 feet tall at the shoulder, with its hump rising 1 foot higher. The two-humped, or Bactrian, camel is suited to cooler, rocky areas. It is stockier, slower (speed 40 feet), and has a higher Constitution score (16).

**Carrying Capacity:** A light load for a camel is up to 300 pounds; a medium load, 301–600 pounds; and a heavy load, 601–900 pounds. A camel can drag 4,500 pounds.

### Combat

\*A camel’s bite is treated as a secondary attack and adds only half the camel’s Strength bonus to the damage roll.','{"full_attack":"Bite +0 melee* (1d4+2*)","environment":"Warm deserts","organization":"Domesticated or herd (6–30)","treasure":"","advancement":"—","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"3d8+6 (19 hp)","hit_points":19,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+10","attack":"Bite +0 melee (1d4+2*)","full_attack":"Bite +0 melee* (1d4+2*)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +5, Ref +6, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"18","dex":"16","con":"14","int":"2","wis":"11","cha":"4"},"skills":"Listen +5, Spot +5","feats":"Alertness, Endurance","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('cat','Cat','Cat','1/4','Tiny','Animal','','1/2 d8 (2 hp)',2,'+2','30 ft. (6 squares)','14 (+2 size, +2 Dex), touch 14, flat-footed 12','+0/–12','Claw +4 melee (1d2–4)','2-1/2 ft./0 ft.','+2','+4','+1',3,15,10,2,12,7,'Balance +10, Climb +6, Hide +14*, Jump +10, Listen +3, Move Silently +6, Spot +3','Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'The statistics presented here describe a common housecat.

### Combat

Cats prefer to sneak up on their prey.

**Skills:** Cats have a +4 racial bonus on Climb, Hide, and Move Silently checks and a +8 racial bonus on Jump checks. Cats have a +8 racial bonus on Balance checks. They use their Dexterity modifier instead of their Strength modifier for Climb and Jump checks. \*In areas of tall grass or heavy undergrowth, the Hide bonus rises to +8.','{"full_attack":"2 claws +4 melee (1d2–4) and bite –1 melee (1d3–4)","environment":"Temperate plains","organization":"Domesticated or solitary","treasure":"","advancement":"—","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1/2 d8 (2 hp)","hit_points":2,"base_attack_grapple":"+0/–12","attack":"Claw +4 melee (1d2–4)","full_attack":"2 claws +4 melee (1d2–4) and bite –1 melee (1d3–4)","space_reach":"2-1/2 ft./0 ft.","saves":"Fort +2, Ref +4, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"3","dex":"15","con":"10","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"7"},"skills":"Balance +10, Climb +6, Hide +14*, Jump +10, Listen +3, Move Silently +6, Spot +3","feats":"Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('cheetah','Cheetah','Cheetah','2','Medium','Animal','','3d8+6 (19 hp)',19,'+4','50 ft. (10 squares)','15 (+4 Dex, +1 natural), touch 14, flat-footed 11','+2/+5','Bite +6 melee','5 ft./5 ft.','+5','+7','+2',16,19,15,2,12,6,'Hide +6, Listen +4, Move Silently +6, Spot +4','Alertness, Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"Trip","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent, sprint"}'::jsonb,'Cheetahs are swift feline predators of the plains. A cheetah is 3 to 5 feet long and weighs 110 to 130 pounds.

### Combat

Cheetahs make sudden sprints to bring down prey.

**Trip (Ex):** A cheetah that hits with a claw or bite attack can attempt to trip the opponent (+3 check modifier) as a free action without making a touch attack or provoking an attack of opportunity. If the attempt fails, the opponent cannot react to trip the cheetah.

**Sprint (Ex):** Once per hour, a cheetah can move ten times its normal speed (500 feet) when it makes a charge.','{"full_attack":"Bite +6 melee (1d6+3) and 2 claws +1 melee (1d2+1)","environment":"Warm plains","organization":"Solitary, pair, or family (3–5)","treasure":"","advancement":"4–5 HD (Medium)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"3d8+6 (19 hp)","hit_points":19,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+5","attack":"Bite +6 melee","full_attack":"Bite +6 melee (1d6+3) and 2 claws +1 melee (1d2+1)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +5, Ref +7, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"16","dex":"19","con":"15","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"6"},"skills":"Hide +6, Listen +4, Move Silently +6, Spot +4","feats":"Alertness, Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"Trip","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent, sprint"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('crocodile','Crocodile','Crocodile','2','Medium','Animal','','3d8+9 (22 hp)',22,'+1','20 ft. (4 squares), swim 30 ft.','15 (+1 Dex, +4 natural), touch 11, flat-footed 14','+2/+6','Bite +6 melee (1d8+6) or tail slap +6 melee (1d12+6)','5 ft./5 ft.','+6','+4','+2',19,12,17,1,12,2,'Hide +7*, Listen +4, Spot +4, Swim +12','Alertness, Skill Focus (Hide)','{"special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Hold breath, low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'Crocodiles are aggressive predators 11 to 12 feet long. They lie mostly submerged in rivers or marshes, with only their eyes and nostrils showing, waiting for prey to come within reach.

### Combat

**Improved Grab (Ex):** To use this ability, a crocodile must hit with its bite attack. It can then attempt to start a grapple as a free action without provoking an attack of opportunity. If it wins the grapple check, the crocodile establishes a hold on the opponent with its mouth and drags it into deep water, attempting to pin it to the bottom.

**Hold Breath (Ex):** A crocodile can hold its breath for a number of rounds equal to 4 x its Constitution score before it risks drowning.

**Skills:** A crocodile has a +8 racial bonus on any Swim check to perform some special action or avoid a hazard. It can always choose to take 10 on a Swim check, even if distracted or endangered. It can use the run action while swimming, provided it swims in a straight line. \*A crocodile gains a +4 racial bonus on Hide checks when in the water. Further, a crocodile can lie in the water with only its eyes and nostrils showing, gaining a +10 cover bonus on Hide checks.','{"full_attack":"Bite +6 melee (1d8+6) or tail slap +6 melee (1d12+6)","environment":"Warm marshes","organization":"Solitary or colony (6–11)","treasure":"","advancement":"4–5 HD (Medium)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"3d8+9 (22 hp)","hit_points":22,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+6","attack":"Bite +6 melee (1d8+6) or tail slap +6 melee (1d12+6)","full_attack":"Bite +6 melee (1d8+6) or tail slap +6 melee (1d12+6)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +6, Ref +4, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"19","dex":"12","con":"17","int":"1","wis":"12","cha":"2"},"skills":"Hide +7*, Listen +4, Spot +4, Swim +12","feats":"Alertness, Skill Focus (Hide)","special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Hold breath, low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('crocodile_giant','Crocodile, Giant','Crocodile, Giant','4','Huge','Animal','','7d8+28 (59 hp)',59,'+1','20 ft. (4 squares), swim 30 ft.','16 (–2 size, +1 Dex, +7 natural), touch 9, flat-footed 15','+5/+21','Bite +11 melee (2d8+12) or tail slap +11 melee (1d12+12)','15 ft./10 ft.','+9','+6','+3',27,12,19,1,12,2,'Hide +1*, Listen +5, Spot +5, Swim +16','Alertness, Endurance, Skill Focus (Hide)','{"special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Hold breath, low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'These huge creatures usually live in salt water and can be more than 20 feet long.

Giant crocodiles fight and behave like their smaller cousins.','{"full_attack":"Bite +11 melee (2d8+12) or tail slap +11 melee (1d12+12)","environment":"Warm marshes","organization":"Solitary or colony (6–11)","treasure":"","advancement":"8–14 HD (Huge)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"7d8+28 (59 hp)","hit_points":59,"base_attack_grapple":"+5/+21","attack":"Bite +11 melee (2d8+12) or tail slap +11 melee (1d12+12)","full_attack":"Bite +11 melee (2d8+12) or tail slap +11 melee (1d12+12)","space_reach":"15 ft./10 ft.","saves":"Fort +9, Ref +6, Will +3","abilities":{"str":"27","dex":"12","con":"19","int":"1","wis":"12","cha":"2"},"skills":"Hide +1*, Listen +5, Spot +5, Swim +16","feats":"Alertness, Endurance, Skill Focus (Hide)","special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Hold breath, low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('dog','Dog','Dog','1/3','Small','Animal','','1d8+2 (6 hp)',6,'+3','40 ft. (8 squares)','15 (+1 size, +3 Dex, +1 natural), touch 14, flat-footed 12','+0/–3','Bite +2 melee (1d4+1)','5 ft./5 ft.','+4','+5','+1',13,17,15,2,12,6,'Jump +7, Listen +5, Spot +5, Survival +1*','Alertness, TrackB','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'The statistics presented here describe a fairly small dog of about 20 to 50 pounds in weight. They also can be used for small wild canines such as coyotes, jackals, and African wild dogs.

### Combat

Dogs generally hunt in packs, chasing and exhausting prey until they can drag it down.

