**Carrying Capacity:** A light load for a light warhorse is up to 230 pounds; a medium load, 231–460 pounds; and a heavy load, 461–690 pounds. A light warhorse can drag 3,450 pounds.','{"full_attack":"2 hooves +6 melee (1d6+4) and bite +1 melee (1d4+2)","environment":"Temperate plains","organization":"Domesticated","treasure":"","advancement":"—","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"4d8+12 (30 hp)","hit_points":30,"base_attack_grapple":"+3/+11","attack":"Hoof +6 melee (1d6+4)","full_attack":"2 hooves +6 melee (1d6+4) and bite +1 melee (1d4+2)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +7, Ref +5, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"18","dex":"13","con":"17","int":"2","wis":"13","cha":"6"},"skills":"Listen +5, Spot +4","feats":"Endurance, Run","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
