**Carrying Capacity:** A light load for a light warhorse is up to 230 pounds; a medium load, 231–460 pounds; and a heavy load, 461–690 pounds. A light warhorse can drag 3,450 pounds.','{"full_attack":"2 hooves +4 melee (1d4+3) and bite –1 melee (1d3+1)","environment":"Temperate plains","organization":"Domesticated","treasure":"","advancement":"—","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"3d8+9 (22 hp)","hit_points":22,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+9","attack":"Hoof +4 melee (1d4+3)","full_attack":"2 hooves +4 melee (1d4+3) and bite –1 melee (1d3+1)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +6, Ref +4, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"16","dex":"13","con":"17","int":"2","wis":"13","cha":"6"},"skills":"Listen +4, Spot +4","feats":"Endurance, Run","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('hyena','Hyena','Hyena','1','Medium','Animal','','2d8+4 (13 hp)',13,'+2','50 ft. (10 squares)','14 (+2 Dex, +2 natural), touch 12, flat-footed 12','+1/+3','Bite +3 melee (1d6+3)','5 ft./5 ft.','+5','+5','+1',14,15,15,2,13,6,'Hide +3*, Listen +6, Spot +4','Alertness','{"special_attacks":"Trip","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'Hyenas are pack hunters infamous for their cunning and their unnerving vocalizations. The statistics presented here are for a striped hyena, which is about 3 feet long and weighs about 120 pounds.

### Combat

A favorite tactic is to send a few individuals against the foe’s front while the rest of the pack circles and attacks from the flanks or rear.

**Trip (Ex):** A hyena that hits with its bite attack can attempt to trip the opponent (+2 check modifier) as a free action without making a touch attack or provoking an attack of opportunity. If the attempt fails, the opponent cannot react to trip the hyena.

**Skills:** \*Hyenas have a +4 racial bonus on Hide checks in areas of tall grass or heavy undergrowth.','{"full_attack":"Bite +3 melee (1d6+3)","environment":"Warm deserts","organization":"Solitary, pair, or pack (7–16)","treasure":"","advancement":"3 HD (Medium); 4–5 HD (Large)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"2d8+4 (13 hp)","hit_points":13,"base_attack_grapple":"+1/+3","attack":"Bite +3 melee (1d6+3)","full_attack":"Bite +3 melee (1d6+3)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +5, Ref +5, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"14","dex":"15","con":"15","int":"2","wis":"13","cha":"6"},"skills":"Hide +3*, Listen +6, Spot +4","feats":"Alertness","special_attacks":"Trip","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('leopard','Leopard','Leopard','2','Medium','Animal','','3d8+6 (19 hp)',19,'+4','40 ft (8 squares), climb 20 ft.','15 (+4 Dex, +1 natural), touch 14, flat-footed 11','+2/+5','Bite +6 melee (1d6+3)','5 ft./5 ft.','+5','+7','+2',16,19,15,2,12,6,'Balance +12, Climb +11, Hide +8*, Jump +11, Listen +6, Move Silently +8, Spot +6','Alertness, Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"Improved grab, pounce, rake 1d3+1","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'These jungle cats are about 4 feet long and weigh about 120 pounds. They usually hunt at night. The statistics presented here can describe any feline of similar size, such as jaguars, panthers, and mountain lions.

### Combat

**Improved Grab (Ex):** To use this ability, a leopard must hit with its bite attack. It can then attempt to start a grapple as a free action without provoking an attack of opportunity. If it wins the grapple check, it establishes a hold and can rake.

**Pounce (Ex):** If a leopard charges a foe, it can make a full attack, including two rake attacks.

**Rake (Ex):** Attack bonus +6 melee, damage 1d3+1.

**Skills:** Leopards have a +8 racial bonus on Jump checks and a +4 racial bonus on Hide and Move Silently checks. Leopards have a +8 racial bonus on Balance and Climb checks. A leopard can always choose to take 10 on a Climb check, even if rushed or threatened. \*In areas of tall grass or heavy undergrowth, the Hide bonus improves to +8.','{"full_attack":"Bite +6 melee (1d6+3) and 2 claws +1 melee (1d3+1)","environment":"Warm forests","organization":"Solitary or pair","treasure":"","advancement":"4–5 HD (Medium)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"3d8+6 (19 hp)","hit_points":19,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+5","attack":"Bite +6 melee (1d6+3)","full_attack":"Bite +6 melee (1d6+3) and 2 claws +1 melee (1d3+1)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +5, Ref +7, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"16","dex":"19","con":"15","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"6"},"skills":"Balance +12, Climb +11, Hide +8*, Jump +11, Listen +6, Move Silently +8, Spot +6","feats":"Alertness, Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"Improved grab, pounce, rake 1d3+1","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('lion','Lion','Lion','3','Large','Animal','','5d8+10 (32 hp)',32,'+3','40 ft. (8 squares)','15 (–1 size, +3 Dex, +3 natural), touch 12, flat-footed 12','+3/+12','Claw +7 melee (1d4+5)','10 ft./5 ft.','+6','+7','+2',21,17,15,2,12,6,'Balance +7, Hide +3*, Listen +5, Move Silently +11, Spot +5','Alertness, Run','{"special_attacks":"Pounce, improved grab, rake 1d4+2","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'The statistics presented here describe a male African lion, which is 5 to 8 feet long and weighs 330 to 550 pounds. Females are slightly smaller but use the same statistics.

### Combat

**Pounce (Ex):** If a lion charges a foe, it can make a full attack, including two rake attacks.

**Improved Grab (Ex):** To use this ability, a lion must hit with its bite attack. It can then attempt to start a grapple as a free action without provoking an attack of opportunity. If it wins the grapple check, it establishes a hold and can rake.

**Rake (Ex):** Attack bonus +7 melee, damage 1d4+2.

**Skills:** Lions have a +4 racial bonus on Balance, Hide, and Move Silently checks. \*In areas of tall grass or heavy undergrowth, the Hide bonus improves to +12.','{"full_attack":"2 claws +7 melee (1d4+5) and bite +2 melee (1d8+2)","environment":"Warm plains","organization":"Solitary, pair, or pride (6–10)","treasure":"","advancement":"6–8 HD (Large)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"5d8+10 (32 hp)","hit_points":32,"base_attack_grapple":"+3/+12","attack":"Claw +7 melee (1d4+5)","full_attack":"2 claws +7 melee (1d4+5) and bite +2 melee (1d8+2)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +6, Ref +7, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"21","dex":"17","con":"15","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"6"},"skills":"Balance +7, Hide +3*, Listen +5, Move Silently +11, Spot +5","feats":"Alertness, Run","special_attacks":"Pounce, improved grab, rake 1d4+2","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('lizard','Lizard','Lizard','1/6','Tiny','Animal','','1/2 d8 (2 hp)',2,'+2','20 ft. (4 squares), climb 20 ft.','14 (+2 size, +2 Dex), touch 14, flat-footed 12','+0/–12','Bite +4 melee (1d4–4)','2-1/2 ft./0 ft.','+2','+4','+1',3,15,10,1,12,2,'Balance +10, Climb +12, Hide +10, Listen +3, Spot +3','Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'The statistics presented here describe small, nonvenomous lizards of perhaps a foot or two in length, such as an iguana.

### Combat

Lizards prefer flight to combat, but they can bite painfully if there is no other option.

**Skills:** Lizards have a +8 racial bonus on Balance checks. They also have a +8 racial bonus on Climb checks and can always choose to take 10 on Climb checks, even if rushed or threatened. Lizards use their Dexterity modifier instead of their Strength modifier for Climb checks.','{"full_attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d4–4)","environment":"Warm forests","organization":"Solitary","treasure":"","advancement":"—","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1/2 d8 (2 hp)","hit_points":2,"base_attack_grapple":"+0/–12","attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d4–4)","full_attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d4–4)","space_reach":"2-1/2 ft./0 ft.","saves":"Fort +2, Ref +4, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"3","dex":"15","con":"10","int":"1","wis":"12","cha":"2"},"skills":"Balance +10, Climb +12, Hide +10, Listen +3, Spot +3","feats":"Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('lizard_monitor','Lizard, Monitor','Lizard, Monitor','2','Medium','Animal','','3d8+9 (22 hp)',22,'+2','30 ft. (6 squares), swim 30 ft.','15 (+2 Dex, +3 natural), touch 12, flat-footed 13','+2/+5','Bite +5 melee (1d8+4)','5 ft./5 ft.','+8','+5','+2',17,15,17,1,12,2,'Climb +7, Hide +6*, Listen +4, Move Silently +6, Spot +4, Swim +11','Alertness, Great Fortitude','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'This category includes fairly large, carnivorous lizards from 3 to 5 feet long.

### Combat

Monitor lizards can be aggressive, using their powerful jaws to tear at prey or enemies.

**Skills:** A monitor lizard has a +8 racial bonus on any Swim check to perform some special action or avoid a hazard. It can always choose to take 10 on a Swim check, even if distracted or endangered. It can use the run action while swimming, provided it swims in a straight line. Monitor lizards have a +4 racial bonus on Hide and Move Silently checks. \*In forested or overgrown areas, the Hide bonus improves to +8.','{"full_attack":"Bite +5 melee (1d8+4)","environment":"Warm forests","organization":"Solitary","treasure":"","advancement":"4–5 HD (Medium)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"3d8+9 (22 hp)","hit_points":22,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+5","attack":"Bite +5 melee (1d8+4)","full_attack":"Bite +5 melee (1d8+4)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +8, Ref +5, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"17","dex":"15","con":"17","int":"1","wis":"12","cha":"2"},"skills":"Climb +7, Hide +6*, Listen +4, Move Silently +6, Spot +4, Swim +11","feats":"Alertness, Great Fortitude","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('manta_ray','Manta Ray','Manta Ray','1','Large','Animal (Aquatic)','','4d8 (18 hp)',18,'+0','Swim 30 ft. (6 squares)','12 (–1 size, +3 natural), touch 9, flat-footed 12','+3/+9','Ram –1 melee* (1d6+1)','10 ft./5 ft.','+4','+4','+2',15,11,10,1,12,2,'Listen +7, Spot +6, Swim +10','Alertness, Endurance','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'These fish are nonaggressive and generally avoid contact with other creatures. They filter plankton and similar small organisms from the water through their gaping, toothless maws.

### Combat

\*If threatened, a manta ray uses its size and weight to ram opponents. This is treated as a secondary attack.

**Skills:** A manta ray has a +8 racial bonus on any Swim check to perform some special action or avoid a hazard. It can always choose to take 10 on a Swim check, even if distracted or endangered. It can use the run action while swimming, provided it swims in a straight line.','{"full_attack":"Ram –1 melee* (1d6+1)","environment":"Warm aquatic","organization":"Solitary or school (2–5)","treasure":"","advancement":"5–6 HD (Medium)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"4d8 (18 hp)","hit_points":18,"base_attack_grapple":"+3/+9","attack":"Ram –1 melee* (1d6+1)","full_attack":"Ram –1 melee* (1d6+1)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +4, Ref +4, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"15","dex":"11","con":"10","int":"1","wis":"12","cha":"2"},"skills":"Listen +7, Spot +6, Swim +10","feats":"Alertness, Endurance","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('monkey','Monkey','Monkey','1/6','Tiny','Animal','','1d8 (4 hp)',4,'+2','30 ft. (6 squares), climb 30 ft.','14 (+2 size, +2 Dex), touch 14, flat-footed 12','+0/–12','Bite +4 melee (1d3–4)','2-1/2 ft./0 ft.','+2','+4','+1',3,15,10,2,12,5,'Balance + 10, Climb +10, Hide +10, Listen +3, Spot +3','Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'The statistics presented here can describe any arboreal monkey that is no bigger than a housecat, such as a colobus or capuchin.

### Combat

Monkeys generally flee into the safety of the trees, but if cornered can fight ferociously.

**Skills:** Monkeys have a +8 racial bonus on Balance and Climb checks. They can always choose to take 10 on Climb checks, even if rushed or threatened. They use their Dexterity modifier instead of their Strength modifier for Climb checks.','{"full_attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d3–4)","environment":"Warm forests","organization":"Troop (10–40)","treasure":"","advancement":"2–3 HD (Small)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1d8 (4 hp)","hit_points":4,"base_attack_grapple":"+0/–12","attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d3–4)","full_attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d3–4)","space_reach":"2-1/2 ft./0 ft.","saves":"Fort +2, Ref +4, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"3","dex":"15","con":"10","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"5"},"skills":"Balance + 10, Climb +10, Hide +10, Listen +3, Spot +3","feats":"Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('mule','Mule','Mule','1','Large','Animal','','3d8+9 (22 hp)',22,'+1','30 ft. (6 squares)','13 (–1 size, +1 Dex, +3 natural), touch 10, flat-footed 12','+2/+9','Hoof +4 melee (1d4+3)','10 ft./5 ft.','+6','+4','+1',16,13,17,2,11,6,'Listen +6, Spot +6','Alertness, Endurance','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'Mules are sterile crossbreeds of donkeys and horses. A mule is similar to a light horse, but slightly stronger and more agile.

### Combat

A mule’s powerful kick can be dangerous.

**Carrying Capacity:** A light load for a mule is up to 230 pounds; a medium load, 231–460 pounds; and a heavy load, 461–690 pounds. A mule can drag 3,450 pounds.

**Skills:** Mules have a +2 racial bonus on Dexterity checks to avoid slipping or falling.','{"full_attack":"2 hooves +4 melee (1d4+3)","environment":"Warm plains","organization":"Domesticated","treasure":"","advancement":"—","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"3d8+9 (22 hp)","hit_points":22,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+9","attack":"Hoof +4 melee (1d4+3)","full_attack":"2 hooves +4 melee (1d4+3)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +6, Ref +4, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"16","dex":"13","con":"17","int":"2","wis":"11","cha":"6"},"skills":"Listen +6, Spot +6","feats":"Alertness, Endurance","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('octopus','Octopus','Octopus','1','Small','Animal (Aquatic)','','2d8 (9 hp)',9,'+3','20 ft. (4 squares), swim 30 ft.','16 (+1 size, +3 Dex, +2 natural), touch 14, flat-footed 13','+1/+2','Arms +5 melee (0)','5 ft./5 ft.','+3','+6','+1',12,17,11,2,12,3,'Escape Artist +13, Hide +11, Listen +2, Spot +5, Swim +9','Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Ink cloud, jet, low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'These bottom-dwelling sea creatures are dangerous only to their prey. If disturbed, they usually try to escape.

### Combat

**Improved Grab (Ex):** To use this ability, an octopus must hit an opponent of any size with its arms attack. It can then attempt to start a grapple as a free action without provoking an attack of opportunity. If it wins the grapple check, it establishes a hold and automatically deals bite damage.

**Ink Cloud (Ex):** An octopus can emit a cloud of jet-black ink 10 feet high by 10 feet wide by 10 feet long once per minute as a free action. The cloud provides total concealment, which the octopus normally uses to escape a losing fight. All vision within the cloud is obscured.

**Jet (Ex):** An octopus can jet backward once per round as a full-round action, at a speed of 200 feet. It must move in a straight line, but does not provoke attacks of opportunity while jetting.

**Skills:** An octopus can change colors, giving it a +4 racial bonus on Hide checks. An octopus also can squeeze and contort its body, giving it a +10 racial bonus on Escape Artist checks. An octopus has a +8 racial bonus on any Swim check to perform some special action or avoid a hazard. It can always choose to take 10 on a Swim check, even if distracted or endangered. It can use the run action while swimming, provided it swims in a straight line.','{"full_attack":"Arms +5 melee (0) and bite +0 melee (1d3)","environment":"Warm aquatic","organization":"Solitary","treasure":"","advancement":"3–6 HD (Medium)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"2d8 (9 hp)","hit_points":9,"base_attack_grapple":"+1/+2","attack":"Arms +5 melee (0)","full_attack":"Arms +5 melee (0) and bite +0 melee (1d3)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +3, Ref +6, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"12","dex":"17","con":"11","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"3"},"skills":"Escape Artist +13, Hide +11, Listen +2, Spot +5, Swim +9","feats":"Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Ink cloud, jet, low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('octopus_giant','Octopus, Giant','Octopus, Giant','8','Large','Animal (Aquatic)','','8d8+11 (47 hp)',47,'+2','20 ft. (4 squares), swim 30 ft.','18 (–1 size, +2 Dex, +7 natural), touch 11, flat-footed 16','+6/+15','Tentacle +10 melee (1d4+5)','10 ft./10 ft. (20 ft. with tentacle)','+7','+8','+3',20,15,13,2,12,3,'Escape Artist +12, Hide +12, Listen +4, Spot +6, Swim +13','Alertness, Skill Focus (Hide), Toughness','{"special_attacks":"Improved grab, constrict","special_qualities":"Ink cloud, jet, low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'These creatures are aggressive and territorial hunters, with arms reaching 10 feet or more in length. Their tentacles are studded with barbs and sharp-edged suckers.

### Combat

An opponent can attack a giant octopus’s tentacles with a sunder attempt as if they were weapons. A giant octopus’s tentacles have 10 hit points each. If a giant octopus is currently grappling a target with the tentacle that is being attacked, it usually uses another limb to make its attack of opportunity against the opponent making the sunder attempt. Severing one of a giant octopus’s tentacles deals 5 points of damage to the creature. A giant octopus usually withdraws from combat if it loses four tentacles. The creature regrows severed limbs in 1d10+10 days.

**Constrict (Ex):** A giant octopus deals 2d8+6 points of damage with a successful grapple check.

**Improved Grab (Ex):** To use this ability, a giant octopus must hit an opponent of any size with a tentacle attack. It can then attempt to start a grapple as a free action without provoking an attack of opportunity. If it wins the grapple check, it establishes a hold and can constrict.

**Ink Cloud (Ex):** A giant octopus can emit a cloud of jet-black ink 20 feet high by 20 feet wide by 20 feet long once per minute as a free action. The cloud provides total concealment, which the octopus normally uses to escape a losing fight. All vision within the cloud is obscured.

**Jet (Ex):** A giant octopus can jet backward once per round as a full-round action, at a speed of 200 feet. It must move in a straight line, but does not provoke attacks of opportunity while jetting.

**Skills:** A giant octopus can change colors, giving it a +4 racial bonus on Hide checks. A giant octopus also can squeeze and contort its body, giving it a +10 racial bonus on Escape Artist checks. A giant octopus has a +8 racial bonus on any Swim check to perform some special action or avoid a hazard. It can always choose to take 10 on a Swim check, even if distracted or endangered. It can use the run action while swimming, provided it swims in a straight line.','{"full_attack":"8 tentacles +10 melee (1d4+5) and bite +5 melee (1d8+2)","environment":"Warm aquatic","organization":"Solitary","treasure":"","advancement":"9–12 HD (Large); 13–24 HD (Huge)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"8d8+11 (47 hp)","hit_points":47,"base_attack_grapple":"+6/+15","attack":"Tentacle +10 melee (1d4+5)","full_attack":"8 tentacles +10 melee (1d4+5) and bite +5 melee (1d8+2)","space_reach":"10 ft./10 ft. (20 ft. with tentacle)","saves":"Fort +7, Ref +8, Will +3","abilities":{"str":"20","dex":"15","con":"13","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"3"},"skills":"Escape Artist +12, Hide +12, Listen +4, Spot +6, Swim +13","feats":"Alertness, Skill Focus (Hide), Toughness","special_attacks":"Improved grab, constrict","special_qualities":"Ink cloud, jet, low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('owl','Owl','Owl','1/4','Tiny','Animal','','1d8 (4 hp)',4,'+3','10 ft. (2 squares), fly 40 ft. (average)','17 (+2 size, +3 Dex, +2 natural), touch 15, flat-footed 14','+0/–11','Talons +5 melee (1d4–3)','2-1/2 ft./0 ft.','+2','+5','+2',4,17,10,2,14,4,'Listen +14, Move Silently +17, Spot +6*','Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'The statistics presented here describe nocturnal birds of prey from 1 to 2 feet long, with wingspans up to 6 feet. They combine both talons into a single attack.

### Combat

Owls swoop quietly down onto prey, attacking with their powerful talons.

**Skills:** Owls have a +8 racial bonus on Listen checks and a +14 racial bonus on Move Silently checks. \*They have a +8 racial bonus on Spot checks in areas of shadowy illumination.','{"full_attack":"Talons +5 melee (1d4–3)","environment":"Temperate forests","organization":"Solitary","treasure":"","advancement":"2 HD (Small)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1d8 (4 hp)","hit_points":4,"base_attack_grapple":"+0/–11","attack":"Talons +5 melee (1d4–3)","full_attack":"Talons +5 melee (1d4–3)","space_reach":"2-1/2 ft./0 ft.","saves":"Fort +2, Ref +5, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"4","dex":"17","con":"10","int":"2","wis":"14","cha":"4"},"skills":"Listen +14, Move Silently +17, Spot +6*","feats":"Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('pony','Pony','Pony','1/4','Medium','Animal','','2d8+2 (11 hp)',11,'+1','40 ft. (8 squares)','13 (+1 Dex, +2 natural), touch 11, flat-footed 12','+1/+2','Hoof –3 melee (1d3*)','5 ft./5 ft.','+4','+4','+0',13,13,12,2,11,4,'Listen +5, Spot +5','Endurance','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'The statistics presented here describe a small horse, under 5 feet tall at the shoulder. Ponies are otherwise similar to light horses and cannot fight while carrying a rider.

### Combat

\*A pony not trained for war does not normally use its hooves to attack but rather to run. Its hoof attack is treated as a secondary attack and adds only half the pony’s Strength bonus to damage.

**Carrying Capacity:** A light load for a pony is up to 75 pounds; a medium load, 76–150 pounds; and a heavy load, 151–225 pounds. A pony can drag 1,125 pounds.','{"full_attack":"2 hooves –3 melee (1d3*)","environment":"Temperate plains","organization":"Solitary","treasure":"","advancement":"—","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"2d8+2 (11 hp)","hit_points":11,"base_attack_grapple":"+1/+2","attack":"Hoof –3 melee (1d3*)","full_attack":"2 hooves –3 melee (1d3*)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +4, Ref +4, Will +0","abilities":{"str":"13","dex":"13","con":"12","int":"2","wis":"11","cha":"4"},"skills":"Listen +5, Spot +5","feats":"Endurance","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('pony_war','Pony, War','Pony, War','1/2','Medium','Animal','','2d8+4 (13 hp)',13,'+1','40 ft. (8 squares)','13 (+1 Dex, +2 natural), touch 11, flat-footed 12','+1/+3','Hoof +3 melee (1d3+2)','5 ft./5 ft.','+5','+4','+0',15,13,14,2,11,4,'Listen +5, Spot +5','Endurance','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'Warponies are bred for strength and aggression, and are similar to light warhorses.

### Combat

A warpony can fight while carrying a rider, but the rider cannot also attack unless he or she succeeds on a Ride check.

**Carrying Capacity:** A light load for a warpony is up to 100 pounds; a medium load, 101–200 pounds; and a heavy load, 201–300 pounds. A warpony can drag 1,500 pounds.','{"full_attack":"2 hooves +3 melee (1d3+2)","environment":"Temperate plains","organization":"Domesticated","treasure":"","advancement":"—","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"2d8+4 (13 hp)","hit_points":13,"base_attack_grapple":"+1/+3","attack":"Hoof +3 melee (1d3+2)","full_attack":"2 hooves +3 melee (1d3+2)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +5, Ref +4, Will +0","abilities":{"str":"15","dex":"13","con":"14","int":"2","wis":"11","cha":"4"},"skills":"Listen +5, Spot +5","feats":"Endurance","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('porpoise','Porpoise','Porpoise','1/2','Medium','Animal','','2d8+2 (11 hp)',11,'+3','Swim 80 ft. (16 squares)','15 (+3 Dex, +2 natural), touch 13, flat-footed 12','+1/+1','Slam +4 melee (2d4)','5 ft./5 ft.','+4','+6','+1',11,17,13,2,12,6,'Listen +8*, Spot +7*, Swim +8','Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Blindsight 120 ft., hold breath, low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'Porpoises are mammals that tend to be playful, friendly, and helpful. A typical porpoise is 4 to 6 feet long and weighs 110 to 160 pounds. The statistics presented here can describe any small whale of similar size.

### Combat

**Blindsight (Ex):** Porpoises can “see” by emitting high-frequency sounds, inaudible to most other creatures, that allow them to locate objects and creatures within 120 feet. A _silence_ spell negates this and forces the porpoise to rely on its vision, which is approximately as good as a human’s.

**Hold Breath (Ex):** A porpoise can hold its breath for a number of rounds equal to 6 x its Constitution score before it risks drowning.

**Skills:** A porpoise has a +8 racial bonus on any Swim check to perform some special action or avoid a hazard. It can always choose to take 10 on a Swim check, even if distracted or endangered. It can use the run action while swimming, provided it swims in a straight line. \*A porpoise has a +4 racial bonus on Spot and Listen checks. These bonuses are lost if its blindsight is negated.','{"full_attack":"Slam +4 melee (2d4)","environment":"Temperate aquatic","organization":"Solitary, pair, or school (3–20)","treasure":"","advancement":"3–4 HD (Medium); 5–6 HD (Large)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"2d8+2 (11 hp)","hit_points":11,"base_attack_grapple":"+1/+1","attack":"Slam +4 melee (2d4)","full_attack":"Slam +4 melee (2d4)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +4, Ref +6, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"11","dex":"17","con":"13","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"6"},"skills":"Listen +8*, Spot +7*, Swim +8","feats":"Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Blindsight 120 ft., hold breath, low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('rat','Rat','Rat','1/8','Tiny','Animal','','1/4 d8 (1 hp)',1,'+2','15 ft. (3 squares), climb 15 ft., swim 15 ft.','14 (+2 size, +2 Dex), touch 14, flat-footed 12','+0/–12','Bite +4 melee (1d3–4)','2-1/2 ft./0 ft.','+2','+4','+1',2,15,10,2,12,2,'Balance +10, Climb +12, Hide +14, Move Silently +10, Swim +10','Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"}'::jsonb,'These omnivorous rodents thrive almost anywhere.

### Combat

Rats usually run away. They bite only as a last resort.

**Skills:** Rats have a +4 racial bonus on Hide and Move Silently checks, and a +8 racial bonus on Balance, Climb, and Swim checks. A rat can always choose to take 10 on Climb checks, even if rushed or threatened. A rat uses its Dexterity modifier instead of its Strength modifier for Climb and Swim checks. A rat has a +8 racial bonus on any Swim check to perform some special action or avoid a hazard. It can always choose to take 10 on a Swim check, even if distracted or endangered. It can use the run action while swimming, provided it swims in a straight line.','{"full_attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d3–4)","environment":"Any","organization":"Plague (10–100)","treasure":"","advancement":"—","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1/4 d8 (1 hp)","hit_points":1,"base_attack_grapple":"+0/–12","attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d3–4)","full_attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d3–4)","space_reach":"2-1/2 ft./0 ft.","saves":"Fort +2, Ref +4, Will +1","abilities":{"str":"2","dex":"15","con":"10","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"2"},"skills":"Balance +10, Climb +12, Hide +14, Move Silently +10, Swim +10","feats":"Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision, scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('raven','Raven','Raven','1/6','Tiny','Animal','','1/4 d8 (1 hp)',1,'+2','10 ft. (2 squares), fly 40 ft. (average)','14 (+2 size, +2 Dex), touch 14, flat-footed 12','+0/–13','Claws +4 melee (1d2–5)','2-1/2 ft./0 ft.','+2','+4','+2',1,15,10,2,14,6,'Listen +3, Spot +5','Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'These glossy black birds are about 2 feet long and have wingspans of about 4 feet. They combine both claws into a single attack. The statistics presented here can describe most nonpredatory birds of similar size.','{"full_attack":"Claws +4 melee (1d2–5)","environment":"Temperate forests","organization":"Solitary","treasure":"","advancement":"—","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"1/4 d8 (1 hp)","hit_points":1,"base_attack_grapple":"+0/–13","attack":"Claws +4 melee (1d2–5)","full_attack":"Claws +4 melee (1d2–5)","space_reach":"2-1/2 ft./0 ft.","saves":"Fort +2, Ref +4, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"1","dex":"15","con":"10","int":"2","wis":"14","cha":"6"},"skills":"Listen +3, Spot +5","feats":"Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('rhinoceros','Rhinoceros','Rhinoceros','4','Large','Animal','','8d8+40 (76 hp)',76,'+0','30 ft. (6 squares)','16 (–1 size, +7 natural), touch 9, flat-footed 16','+6/+18','Gore +13 melee (2d6+12)','10 ft./5 ft.','+11','+6','+3',26,10,21,2,13,2,'Listen +14, Spot +3','Alertness, Endurance, Improved Natural Attack (gore)','{"special_attacks":"Powerful charge","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'The rhinoceros is infamous for its bad temper and willingness to charge intruders.

The statistics presented here are based on the African black rhino, which is 6 to 14 feet long, 3 to 6 feet high at the shoulder, and weighs up to 6,000 pounds. These statistics can describe any herbivore of similar size and similar natural weapons (antlers, horns, tusks, or the like).

### Combat

When it is harassed or annoyed, a rhinoceros lowers its head and charges.

**Powerful Charge (Ex):** A rhinoceros deals 4d6+24 points of damage when it makes a charge.','{"full_attack":"Gore +13 melee (2d6+12)","environment":"Warm plains","organization":"Solitary or herd (2–12)","treasure":"","advancement":"9–12 HD (Large); 13–24 HD (Huge)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"8d8+40 (76 hp)","hit_points":76,"base_attack_grapple":"+6/+18","attack":"Gore +13 melee (2d6+12)","full_attack":"Gore +13 melee (2d6+12)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +11, Ref +6, Will +3","abilities":{"str":"26","dex":"10","con":"21","int":"2","wis":"13","cha":"2"},"skills":"Listen +14, Spot +3","feats":"Alertness, Endurance, Improved Natural Attack (gore)","special_attacks":"Powerful charge","special_qualities":"Low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('shark_medium','Shark, Medium','Shark, Medium','1','Medium','Animal (Aquatic)','','3d8+3 (16 hp)',16,'+2','Swim 60 ft. (12 squares)','15 (+2 Dex, +3 natural), touch 12, flat-footed 13','+2/+3','Bite +4 melee (1d6+1)','5 ft./5 ft.','+4','+5','+2',13,15,13,1,12,2,'Listen +6, Spot +6, Swim +9','Alertness, Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Blindsense, keen scent"}'::jsonb,'These carnivorous fish are aggressive and liable to make unprovoked attacks against anything that approaches them. Smaller sharks are from 5 to 8 feet long and not usually dangerous to creatures other than their prey. Large sharks can reach around 15 feet in length and are a serious threat. Huge sharks are true monsters, like great whites, that can exceed 20 feet in length.

### Combat

Sharks circle and observe potential prey, then dart in and bite with their powerful jaws.

**Blindsense (Ex):** A shark can locate creatures underwater within a 30-foot radius. This ability works only when the shark is underwater.

**Keen Scent (Ex):** A shark can notice creatures by scent in a 180-foot radius and detect blood in the water at ranges of up to a mile.

**Skills:** A shark has a +8 racial bonus on any Swim check to perform some special action or avoid a hazard. It can always choose to take 10 on a Swim check, even if distracted or endangered. It can use the run action while swimming, provided it swims in a straight line.','{"full_attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d6+1)","environment":"Cold aquatic","organization":"Solitary, school (2–5), or pack (6–11)","treasure":"","advancement":"4–6 HD (Medium)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"3d8+3 (16 hp)","hit_points":16,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+3","attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d6+1)","full_attack":"Bite +4 melee (1d6+1)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +4, Ref +5, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"13","dex":"15","con":"13","int":"1","wis":"12","cha":"2"},"skills":"Listen +6, Spot +6, Swim +9","feats":"Alertness, Weapon Finesse","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Blindsense, keen scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
