### Combat

Sharks circle and observe potential prey, then dart in and bite with their powerful jaws.

**Blindsense (Ex):** A shark can locate creatures underwater within a 30-foot radius. This ability works only when the shark is underwater.

**Keen Scent (Ex):** A shark can notice creatures by scent in a 180-foot radius and detect blood in the water at ranges of up to a mile.

**Skills:** A shark has a +8 racial bonus on any Swim check to perform some special action or avoid a hazard. It can always choose to take 10 on a Swim check, even if distracted or endangered. It can use the run action while swimming, provided it swims in a straight line.','{"full_attack":"Bite +10 melee (2d6+7)","environment":"Cold aquatic","organization":"Solitary, school (2–5), or pack (6–11)","treasure":"","advancement":"11–17 HD (Huge)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"10d8+20 (65 hp)","hit_points":65,"base_attack_grapple":"+7/+20","attack":"Bite +10 melee (2d6+7)","full_attack":"Bite +10 melee (2d6+7)","space_reach":"15 ft./10 ft.","saves":"Fort +11, Ref +9, Will +4","abilities":{"str":"21","dex":"15","con":"15","int":"1","wis":"12","cha":"2"},"skills":"Listen +10, Spot +10, Swim +13","feats":"Alertness, Great Fortitude, Improved Initiative, Iron Will","special_attacks":"—","special_qualities":"Blindsense, keen scent"},"source_file":"monsters-animals.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-animals.html',true),
('constrictor_snake','Constrictor Snake','Constrictor Snake','2','Medium','Animal','','3d8+6 (19 hp)',19,'+3','20 ft. (4 squares), climb 20 ft., swim 20 ft.','15 (+3 Dex, +2 natural), touch 13, flat-footed 12','+2/+5','Bite +5 melee (1d3+4)','5 ft./5 ft.','+4','+6','+2',17,17,13,1,12,2,'Balance +11, Climb +14, Hide +10, Listen +7, Spot +7, Swim +11','Alertness, Toughness','{"special_attacks":"Constrict 1d3+4, improved grab","special_qualities":"Scent"}'::jsonb,'Constrictor snakes usually are not aggressive and flee when confronted. They hunt for food but do not attempt to make a meal out of any creature that is too large to constrict.

#### Combat

Constrictor snakes hunt by grabbing prey with their mouths and then squeezing it with their powerful bodies.

**Constrict (Ex):** On a successful grapple check, a constrictor snake deals 1d3+4 points of damage.

